{
  "overall_diagnosis": "Both rollouts produce feasible reports but with objective values ~3.6% above the verifier’s known optimal costs, far outside the allowed optimality gap. This strongly suggests a modeling mismatch in the DC-OPF objective/constraints relative to the expected formulation—most likely in economic dispatch cost evaluation (units / coefficient handling / inclusion of constant terms) and/or DC network constraints (B matrix / line flow limits / tap & shift conventions). LMP scaling also appears wrong in one rollout (orders of magnitude too large), indicating dual/units confusion. Skills covering dispatch cost construction, DC power flow conventions, and LMP/dual extraction need repair/clarification to prevent suboptimal or mis-scaled formulations.",
